WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:08.236
Captain's Log, Stardate 53896.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:11.869
B'Elanna Torres
has requested permission

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:18.180
to take the Delta Flyer
and search for dilithium.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:22.517
Shining Voyager, far from home,

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:26.184
far from the gleaming cities
of Earth.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.590
Headstrong B'Elanna Torres

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.423
and young Harry Kim

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:33.557
speed away from Voyager
on the Delta Flyer

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.225
in search of their treasures.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.632
I've trimmed the sails,

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.965
but the sea is rough.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.505
Maybe we should return.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.733
I know what I'm doing.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:47.644
A wave as high as a mountain
struck the Delta Flyer.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.341
Get into the escape pod.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.781
We die together.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.408
No one is going to die.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.975
Go.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:57.649
Young Harry Kim left her side

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:02.923
and B'Elanna Torres
was thrown against the rocks

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:06.432
the rocks of our very shore.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.935
Which is where I,
Kelis the Poet,

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.630
found her...

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.695
broken...

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.967
dying.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.139
She told me her story...

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.038
...and now I've told you.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:41.895
An excellent conceit, that
you discovered her yourself.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.957
Thank you.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.900
Well, now that B'Elanna Torres

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.269
has come to our shore,
what will happen?

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.865
Does Captain Janeway
come searching for her,

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.843
or does she give her up
for lost?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.503
Who can say?

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.104
Well, I would hope that you can.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.183
I want to see more
of these Voyager Eternals.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.447
Inspiration...

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.421
can't be forced.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.754
One week.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.486
Or three weeks.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.618
Uh, maybe two.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.226
One week.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.266
The story will continue.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:18.427
Have you noticed how thin
my performers have gotten?

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.504
Let them eat this.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.820
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.415
our patron salutes you.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.254
Finally!

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.956
We're doing
another Voyager play...

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.999
as soon as I can write it.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.901
Shall we celebrate,
the two of us?

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.404
I have very little time.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.338
Celebrating will have to wait.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:35.940
Who are you?!

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.974
Kelis... Kelis, the Poet.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.822
Your servant.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.424
My servant.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.629
All right.

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:41.196
Then let me go.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:44.243
I... can't.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.971
Why not?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.370
You'll fly from me...

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.043
the way inspiration always does.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.851
You're trying to kill me.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.417
I'm releasing the heat
from your veins.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:03.519
What are you talking about?

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.723
You've been in a fever
since I found you.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.732
Bleeding is the best way
to treat it.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.893
Oh, I can see I'm in good hands.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.732
Something tells me
you have your doubts.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.569
There's a medkit over there.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.070
A box.

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:20.374
Made out of metal?

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.847
There's a small cylinder inside.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.444
Bring it here.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:35.624
Give it to me.

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.436
Don't be afraid.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:47.803
It won't hurt you.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.698
Here.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.974
Pass it over where you cut me.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.760
You're an Eternal.

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:18.463
I suppose such things
are to be expected.

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:21.905
What other things do you
expect from an Eternal?

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:26.104
The power to make the ground
open up and the sky to fall.

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:29.706
All the strange events
sung by the ancient poets.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:32.751
Fortunately for me,
no poet has ever sung

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:34.081
about your clan.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.245
I'm the first.

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:36.413
My clan?

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:39.117
The Eternals on Voyager.

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:42.753
"Shining Voyager,
far from home."

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:44.763
How do you know about that?

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:55.064
Delta Flyer Log,
Stardate 53918.

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:56.165
Harry and I are continuing

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:57.368
toward the fourth planet.

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:59.673
Sensors have picked up
natural dilithium deposits

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:00.939
on nearly every land mass.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.878
Acknowledged.

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.609
Has your warp core been damaged?

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:06.777
Yes. We're running on thrusters.

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:09.185
Can you track our position?

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:11.883
How long have I been here?

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:14.691
Eight days.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.423
I was walking through
these mountains.

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:20.557
I saw a light
burn across the sky,

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:23.227
and I heard a terrible sound.

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.566
When I arrived, I found you.

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:27.435
I treated your wounds.

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:29.441
And you tied me to this chair.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:32.501
When a gift falls
from the heavens,

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:35.206
only a fool would let her go.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:38.250
You've already given me
one play.

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.912
The story told by those voices.

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:43.646
I pieced them together,

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.554
tried to fill in the gaps.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.923
You made a play out of our logs?

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:52.260
The Away Mission
of B'Elanna Torres.

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:54.322
My patron was impressed.

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.291
Well, he has great taste.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.895
Now, take that knife
of yours and cut me free.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:05.668
That... would be unwise.

00:09:05.745 --> 00:09:07.235
Why?

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:10.373
My patron is intrigued
by the Voyager Eternals.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.882
He wants another play.

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:14.476
To compose that, I need more...

00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:15.816
details.

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:18.015
And you expect
to get them from me?

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.650
I did save your life.

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:25.795
I need to get back to Voyager.

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:31.703
I need another play.

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:35.072
What exactly
do you want to know?

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:35.835
Everything.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:37.432
It's not possible.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.740
We "Eternals" have our rules.

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:42.781
We can't just...
give everything away.

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:47.281
How did you get lost?

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:50.322
Cut me free and I'll tell you.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.921
You won't leave me?

00:09:55.995 --> 00:09:57.292
Cut me free.

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:17.312
You're the one who's leaving.

00:10:21.754 --> 00:10:23.745
Don't come back.

00:10:33.366 --> 00:10:36.699
Computer, bring the subspace
transmitter on line.

00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:37.963
Unable to comply.

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:39.163
Why not?

00:10:39.238 --> 00:10:40.671
Insufficient power.

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:52.851
Great. Now there's no power.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:54.852
Are you hungry?

00:10:55.955 --> 00:10:57.889
I told you not to come back.

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:01.555
You haven't eaten in days.

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:04.892
We have to support each other,
we poets.

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:10.962
I'm an Engineer.

00:11:12.672 --> 00:11:14.264
I fix things.

00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:18.467
From the looks of it,
you're not doing so well.

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:20.239
Are you a poet or a critic?

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:25.847
Tell me about Earth.

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:28.944
I have to sing
for my supper, huh?

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:30.318
We all do...

00:11:31.691 --> 00:11:33.318
...in one way or another.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.190
Earth.

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:48.537
It's, uh...

00:11:48.607 --> 00:11:51.974
an island...

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:55.274
a beautiful island,
blue and green.

00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:56.575
And Voyager?

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.207
A-a great ship?

00:11:58.284 --> 00:12:00.718
In a long line of great ships.

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:02.913
How did Voyager get lost?

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:05.320
The Caretaker.

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:07.154
An Eternal.

00:12:08.527 --> 00:12:10.927
Yes, you could say that.

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:12.930
He...

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:16.297
caused a storm,
which blew us off course.

00:12:21.006 --> 00:12:22.132
Tom Paris.

00:12:23.476 --> 00:12:24.943
Are you in love with him?

00:12:25.077 --> 00:12:26.772
Supper is over.

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:32.511
Come with me.

00:13:00.312 --> 00:13:02.872
This is where we put
all the names and dates

00:13:02.948 --> 00:13:05.212
when our heads
won't hold anymore.

00:13:05.284 --> 00:13:06.717
A memory.

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:08.253
Exactly.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.446
Tell me...

00:13:09.522 --> 00:13:11.390
have you ever seen this before?

00:13:15.227 --> 00:13:16.854
Winter's tears.

00:13:18.464 --> 00:13:20.227
Can you get me some?

00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:23.928
This is... dilithium,
isn't it?

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:25.732
What you were looking for.

00:13:25.805 --> 00:13:27.102
Where can I find it?

00:13:27.173 --> 00:13:28.936
The only deposit I know of is

00:13:29.074 --> 00:13:31.406
on the hunting grounds
of my patron.

00:13:31.477 --> 00:13:33.206
He'd execute me for trespassing,

00:13:33.279 --> 00:13:36.043
and you, well, he'd love
to capture an Eternal.

00:13:36.115 --> 00:13:39.846
M-maybe I'm more powerful
than he is.

00:13:39.919 --> 00:13:42.353
Perhaps, but, if he caught you,

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:45.618
he'd force you to fight
against his enemies.

00:13:45.691 --> 00:13:47.886
They're constantly
at each other's throats,

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.393
bickering over territory,

00:13:49.461 --> 00:13:51.759
raiding each other's land,
starting wars

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:54.823
whenever they can be
guaranteed of good weather

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.891
and we suffer the consequences.

00:13:56.969 --> 00:13:59.563
You don't want
to get involved with them.

00:13:59.638 --> 00:14:02.072
Which is why you're going
to get the dilithium.

00:14:02.141 --> 00:14:04.541
I told you,
I'd be executed if I'm caught.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.407
The dilithium...

00:14:06.478 --> 00:14:09.072
or I don't say
another word about...

00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:12.117
"shining Voyager,
far from home."

00:14:15.454 --> 00:14:16.819
Did you?

00:14:20.526 --> 00:14:23.222
Don't get caught.

00:14:38.644 --> 00:14:39.941
Well?

00:14:48.854 --> 00:14:50.116
Beautiful.

00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:54.289
I've got an idea
for your next play.

00:14:55.895 --> 00:14:58.864
I've been visited
by inspiration herself.

00:14:58.931 --> 00:15:00.865
How does this sound?

00:15:00.933 --> 00:15:05.029
The Rescue of B'Elanna Torres...
right here, in one week.

00:15:05.104 --> 00:15:06.036
One week?!

00:15:06.105 --> 00:15:07.504
Let's get to work.

00:15:15.414 --> 00:15:16.506
Dismissed.

00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:18.174
That's it?

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.239
Mr. Paris, try to stay calm.

00:15:19.318 --> 00:15:20.910
No, that's not going to happen.

00:15:21.053 --> 00:15:22.680
Isn't there
anything else we can do?

00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:24.586
Not until something
shows up on sensors.

00:15:24.657 --> 00:15:26.090
I'll take a shuttle out myself.

00:15:26.158 --> 00:15:28.251
I'll run
a planet-by-planet search.

00:15:28.327 --> 00:15:29.794
An inefficient plan.

00:15:29.862 --> 00:15:31.489
And too dangerous.
You could

00:15:31.563 --> 00:15:34.430
be hit by the same spatial
eddies that sent the Flyer

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:35.432
off course.

00:15:35.501 --> 00:15:36.900
We need to concentrate

00:15:36.969 --> 00:15:38.596
our efforts from here, Tom.

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:39.899
All right?

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.238
Dismissed.

00:15:54.119 --> 00:15:55.780
Steady-armed Paris,

00:15:55.854 --> 00:15:58.948
bound by a sleep
that brings no rest...

00:15:59.091 --> 00:16:00.524
The door opens

00:16:00.592 --> 00:16:03.356
and the shadow of a woman
falls on the helmsman.

00:16:03.429 --> 00:16:07.126
His eyes open...

00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:11.499
Seven of Nine,
did you find B'Elanna Torres?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.061
I'm sorry to disappoint you.

00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:15.367
Closer.

00:16:19.712 --> 00:16:21.703
Closer.

00:16:27.119 --> 00:16:28.882
Unpleasant news,

00:16:28.954 --> 00:16:32.617
delivered by the most
pleasing of messengers.

00:16:35.127 --> 00:16:37.721
No, no, no, no.

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:40.697
Seven of Nine is a Borg,

00:16:40.766 --> 00:16:42.495
- the scourge of the Eternals.
- I...

00:16:42.568 --> 00:16:43.830
You're portraying her

00:16:43.902 --> 00:16:45.563
like a shy bride
on her wedding night.

00:16:45.637 --> 00:16:47.264
Once more.

00:16:53.645 --> 00:16:55.374
Seven of Nine,

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:57.938
did you find B'Elanna Torres?

00:16:58.083 --> 00:17:00.881
I am sorry to disappoint you.

00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:07.822
I can't blame my performers.

00:17:07.893 --> 00:17:11.021
These Eternals on Voyager
are difficult to understand.

00:17:11.096 --> 00:17:12.586
Will you stop walking around?

00:17:12.664 --> 00:17:14.291
You're going to break something.

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:15.890
This Tuvok, for example.

00:17:16.035 --> 00:17:18.003
He's not like anybody
I've ever met.

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:19.901
No emotions?
How's that possible?

00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:22.701
It just is.

00:17:24.443 --> 00:17:26.377
It worked?

00:17:26.445 --> 00:17:28.913
It worked.

00:17:42.795 --> 00:17:44.387
Okay.

00:17:44.463 --> 00:17:47.762
Computer, bring subspace
transmitter on line.

00:17:49.468 --> 00:17:50.901
What happened?!

00:17:50.969 --> 00:17:52.402
I don't know.

00:17:52.471 --> 00:17:55.031
The transmitter must have
been weakened in the crash.

00:17:55.107 --> 00:17:57.735
It couldn't take
the energy surge.

00:17:58.977 --> 00:17:59.944
These Vulcans...

00:18:00.045 --> 00:18:01.842
Enough!

00:18:07.586 --> 00:18:10.453
What kind of metallurgic
technology

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:12.513
do you people have?

00:18:12.591 --> 00:18:14.491
Alloys...
which ones can you make?

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.822
Steel? Bronze?

00:18:15.894 --> 00:18:17.361
Bronze.

00:18:17.429 --> 00:18:19.021
Bronze, all right.

00:18:19.098 --> 00:18:22.465
I need a plate of metal
this big, as thin as it can be...

00:18:22.534 --> 00:18:24.263
three parts tin
to five parts bronze,

00:18:24.336 --> 00:18:25.894
one side coated with gold.

00:18:26.004 --> 00:18:28.131
Gold is expensive;
I can't afford it.

00:18:28.207 --> 00:18:29.504
Then you're going into debt.

00:18:29.575 --> 00:18:31.805
Then tell me about the Vulcans.

00:18:31.877 --> 00:18:33.606
Get me the plate,
and then I'll tell you.

00:18:33.679 --> 00:18:35.704
Everyone's asleep.
I'll do it in the morning.

00:18:37.282 --> 00:18:39.978
The Vulcans?

00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:49.890
Maybe I've miscounted, but...

00:18:49.962 --> 00:18:53.056
I don't think you've slept
in ten days?

00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:55.464
Your count is accurate.

00:18:57.736 --> 00:19:00.671
Don't you think
you should go to bed?

00:19:00.739 --> 00:19:04.038
As a Vulcan,
I can function without sleep

00:19:04.109 --> 00:19:06.339
for more than two weeks.

00:19:06.411 --> 00:19:09.039
But there's a point
of diminishing returns

00:19:09.114 --> 00:19:12.015
when your mind starts
to play tricks on you.

00:19:12.084 --> 00:19:17.181
My mind, Mr. Neelix,
does not play tricks.

00:19:21.093 --> 00:19:23.653
The ship is lonely
without them, isn't it?

00:19:23.729 --> 00:19:29.361
If you would allow me
to continue my sensor analysis,

00:19:29.434 --> 00:19:32.164
I might be able to locate them.

00:19:34.106 --> 00:19:37.200
If there's anything else
you need...

00:19:37.276 --> 00:19:40.074
a stronger tea, perhaps.

00:19:46.652 --> 00:19:50.554
When a friend is lost,
the mind is split in half,

00:19:50.622 --> 00:19:52.556
divided between memory
of the past

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:55.115
and fear of the future.

00:19:55.194 --> 00:19:57.890
Harry Kim, Ensign.

00:19:57.963 --> 00:19:59.931
Only a boy when fate took you

00:20:00.032 --> 00:20:02.466
from the arms
of blue-green Earth.

00:20:02.534 --> 00:20:07.403
B'Elanna Torres,
half-Klingon, half-human.

00:20:07.472 --> 00:20:09.303
I am honored to call you...

00:20:09.374 --> 00:20:11.535
What are you doing?

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:13.407
Is that a tear?

00:20:13.478 --> 00:20:15.105
Yes.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:17.273
Logical Tuvok doesn't cry.

00:20:17.349 --> 00:20:19.943
That's why they call him
logical.

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:21.451
Everybody cries.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:22.953
The land of Vulcan

00:20:23.021 --> 00:20:25.421
has no laughter,
and it has no tears.

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:28.584
It is a very quiet place...
calm, just like Tuvok.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.958
I can't believe that.

00:20:31.063 --> 00:20:32.963
You don't have to;
just don't cry.

00:20:33.065 --> 00:20:35.090
The audience
won't believe it either.

00:20:35.167 --> 00:20:37.635
They'll either think Tuvok
is an unfeeling monster

00:20:37.703 --> 00:20:39.398
or that I am a bad performer.

00:20:39.471 --> 00:20:42.133
They'll realize that beneath
your unfeeling exterior

00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:44.300
is a heart
that's breaking, silently

00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:47.243
and in more pain than any of us
can possibly understand,

00:20:47.312 --> 00:20:49.746
because that's what it is
to be Vulcan.

00:20:54.486 --> 00:20:56.147
Try it again.

00:20:57.789 --> 00:20:59.814
Kelis!

00:20:59.891 --> 00:20:59.992
What's wrong?

00:20:59.992 --> 00:21:01.721
What's wrong?

00:21:01.793 --> 00:21:05.320
Our patron has been insulted
by his enemy to the north.

00:21:05.397 --> 00:21:07.262
The armories are opened.

00:21:08.033 --> 00:21:09.057
Has a battlefield been chosen?

00:21:09.134 --> 00:21:10.931
Not yet.

00:21:11.036 --> 00:21:13.402
Then we have a chance.

00:21:25.651 --> 00:21:27.243
I need your help.

00:21:27.319 --> 00:21:29.116
I've given you enough help.

00:21:29.187 --> 00:21:31.121
Where's that piece of metal?

00:21:37.162 --> 00:21:39.096
Not bad.

00:21:39.164 --> 00:21:40.791
My patron's been angered

00:21:40.866 --> 00:21:42.959
by the leader
of a neighboring state.

00:21:43.035 --> 00:21:44.627
He'll want to take revenge.

00:21:44.703 --> 00:21:46.136
It could lead to war.

00:21:46.238 --> 00:21:50.140
We Eternals aren't supposed
to take sides.

00:21:50.208 --> 00:21:52.301
I'm not asking you to fight.

00:21:52.377 --> 00:21:54.811
I need a way to change his mind.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:57.576
I don't have
that kind of magical power.

00:21:57.649 --> 00:21:58.980
Yes, you do.

00:21:59.117 --> 00:22:02.609
I believe
the right kind of play

00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:05.418
can turn the mind
from violent thoughts.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:08.186
The perfect play
might even stop a war.

00:22:11.296 --> 00:22:14.390
I can't fix the transmitter
with this.

00:22:14.466 --> 00:22:16.730
It has too many impurities.

00:22:16.802 --> 00:22:19.270
It'll never carry
a plasma charge.

00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:23.069
If the fighting starts,
scouting parties will start

00:22:23.141 --> 00:22:25.735
moving through these mountains.

00:22:25.811 --> 00:22:27.938
You'll be discovered.

00:22:28.013 --> 00:22:29.503
But my play...

00:22:29.581 --> 00:22:32.448
it could stop it from happening.

00:22:34.152 --> 00:22:36.746
You have to help me.

00:22:36.822 --> 00:22:38.414
There's nothing I can do.

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:39.787
Then come with me.

00:22:39.858 --> 00:22:42.258
I'll show you
what I've done so far.

00:22:44.463 --> 00:22:47.227
It's our only chance.

00:22:49.868 --> 00:22:52.564
She's a fellow poet
from across the eastern sea,

00:22:52.637 --> 00:22:54.605
an expert
on the Voyager Eternals.

00:22:54.673 --> 00:22:56.971
She's devoted her life to them.

00:22:57.109 --> 00:22:59.577
She's here to help.

00:23:09.821 --> 00:23:11.789
The Rescue of B'Elanna Torres.

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:14.325
We begin with Harry Kim,

00:23:14.393 --> 00:23:16.793
reaching Voyager
in the escape pod.

00:23:16.862 --> 00:23:18.830
He tells Captain Janeway

00:23:18.897 --> 00:23:21.422
that B'Elanna Torres is lost.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:23.934
We continue to the point
where they discover

00:23:24.035 --> 00:23:26.367
a piece of the Delta Flyer.

00:23:26.438 --> 00:23:28.406
After that...

00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:31.936
It's simple.

00:23:32.077 --> 00:23:33.567
They search for B'Elanna Torres.

00:23:33.645 --> 00:23:34.907
B'Elanna Torres is found...

00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:37.676
- Or not found.
- Or not found.

00:23:37.749 --> 00:23:38.773
The end.

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.818
Sounds pretty
straightforward to me.

00:23:40.886 --> 00:23:42.683
That's exactly the problem.

00:23:42.754 --> 00:23:44.551
Where is the mistaken identity?

00:23:44.623 --> 00:23:46.716
The discovery?
The sudden reversal?

00:23:48.727 --> 00:23:53.562
Mistaken identity...
a character who is someone else.

00:23:53.632 --> 00:23:55.065
Discovery...

00:23:55.133 --> 00:23:57.465
the moment when that identity
is revealed.

00:23:57.536 --> 00:24:01.165
Reversal... a situation
that turns from good to bad

00:24:01.239 --> 00:24:02.729
in a blink of an eye.

00:24:02.808 --> 00:24:05.675
Find the truth of your story,

00:24:05.744 --> 00:24:09.111
and you won't need
all those tricks.

00:24:09.181 --> 00:24:13.345
I don't know how things are done
across the Eastern Sea,

00:24:13.418 --> 00:24:17.684
but here,
poets have become lazy.

00:24:17.756 --> 00:24:23.160
They rely on manipulation
to move their audience.

00:24:23.228 --> 00:24:25.856
It wasn't always that way.

00:24:25.931 --> 00:24:28.229
Welcome.

00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:29.767
Thank you.

00:24:33.171 --> 00:24:35.230
The truth of my story.

00:24:35.307 --> 00:24:37.571
It's an old-fashioned idea.

00:24:37.642 --> 00:24:41.476
Today audiences want
excitement... passion.

00:24:43.181 --> 00:24:44.910
Let me show you what I've done

00:24:44.983 --> 00:24:47.679
with Captain Janeway
and Commander Chakotay.

00:24:49.354 --> 00:24:52.448
Let's make a good impression
on our visitor.

00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:58.258
Chakotay, why must I be denied

00:24:58.330 --> 00:25:02.494
what every other female officer
on this ship can have?

00:25:02.567 --> 00:25:04.057
Captain?

00:25:04.135 --> 00:25:06.535
The privilege...

00:25:06.605 --> 00:25:08.732
of your touch.

00:25:25.657 --> 00:25:26.817
Come in.

00:25:30.095 --> 00:25:33.258
If that was good news,
you'd be smiling.

00:25:33.331 --> 00:25:36.459
I was just contacted
by an alien transport vessel.

00:25:36.535 --> 00:25:40.301
They picked up
the Delta Flyer's distress call.

00:25:44.175 --> 00:25:46.370
The primary controls
are off-line.

00:25:46.444 --> 00:25:49.106
I've ordered Harry to eject.
I still have thrusters.

00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:51.375
I'm setting a course
for an L-Class planet.

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:52.939
I'll try to maintain contact.

00:25:53.084 --> 00:25:55.416
They couldn't get a fix
on her position.

00:25:55.487 --> 00:25:57.455
That was ten days ago.

00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:01.358
B'Elanna ordered Harry
into an escape pod.

00:26:01.426 --> 00:26:03.291
What's the longest
he could survive?

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:06.362
Less than ten days.

00:26:08.166 --> 00:26:09.690
An L-Class planet.

00:26:09.768 --> 00:26:12.532
I've already narrowed
the search parameters.

00:26:12.604 --> 00:26:15.300
If B'Elanna made it there,
it's possible Harry did, too.

00:26:22.213 --> 00:26:24.306
Good night, Commander.

00:26:24.382 --> 00:26:25.815
Captain.

00:26:36.728 --> 00:26:39.253
We'll have a final rehearsal
in the morning.

00:26:42.867 --> 00:26:46.325
The last Tuvok scene
doesn't make sense to me,

00:26:46.404 --> 00:26:48.929
and we still don't
have an ending.

00:26:49.074 --> 00:26:51.838
I've got the rest of
the night to work on it.

00:26:51.910 --> 00:26:54.378
Maybe you can get some sleep.

00:27:05.523 --> 00:27:06.990
What did you think?

00:27:07.058 --> 00:27:11.051
Captain Janeway kissing
Commander Chakotay?

00:27:11.129 --> 00:27:14.030
Tom Paris kissing Seven of Nine?

00:27:14.099 --> 00:27:16.363
I don't see the point.

00:27:16.434 --> 00:27:18.902
Anger is like fire.

00:27:19.004 --> 00:27:23.134
Love can be the rain
that extinguishes it.

00:27:23.208 --> 00:27:26.541
My patron is filled
with hatred for his rival.

00:27:26.611 --> 00:27:29.444
So our play should be
filled with love.

00:27:29.514 --> 00:27:32.074
You can't change
somebody's way of life

00:27:32.150 --> 00:27:34.118
with a few lines of dialogue.

00:27:34.185 --> 00:27:35.709
Yes, you can.

00:27:35.787 --> 00:27:37.516
It's been done before.

00:27:37.589 --> 00:27:40.854
Do you know
what this place used to be...

00:27:40.925 --> 00:27:42.187
a hundred years ago?

00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:43.522
A temple.

00:27:43.595 --> 00:27:45.927
And this was the altar stone.

00:27:45.997 --> 00:27:48.591
Every year a victim
would be sacrificed on it

00:27:48.667 --> 00:27:49.895
in honor of winter,

00:27:49.968 --> 00:27:52.232
and then one year...

00:27:52.303 --> 00:27:55.238
nobody remembers
exactly when or why...

00:27:55.306 --> 00:27:57.866
a play took the place
of the ritual,

00:27:57.942 --> 00:28:00.433
and no one had to die
here again.

00:28:02.347 --> 00:28:06.374
Why can't my play
take the place of a war?

00:28:06.451 --> 00:28:09.887
Well, you're going to have to do
a lot better than Harry Kim

00:28:10.021 --> 00:28:11.420
kissing the Delaney sisters.

00:28:11.489 --> 00:28:12.456
Why?

00:28:12.524 --> 00:28:15.322
Because...

00:28:15.393 --> 00:28:18.692
when you think that you are
surrounded by enemies,

00:28:18.763 --> 00:28:22.028
when you're up against the Borg,
or... or Species 8472,

00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:26.628
the last thing on your mind
is romance.

00:28:26.705 --> 00:28:28.696
You're an Eternal.

00:28:30.041 --> 00:28:31.599
You have to help me.

00:28:36.748 --> 00:28:38.841
I'm sorry, Kelis.

00:28:38.917 --> 00:28:40.976
The Borg...

00:28:42.987 --> 00:28:45.114
tell me more about them.

00:28:48.126 --> 00:28:53.894
They are soldiers,
part of a vast army.

00:28:53.965 --> 00:28:56.433
They all think the same thoughts

00:28:56.501 --> 00:29:01.461
and they travel on ships
that look like hives.

00:29:01.539 --> 00:29:03.370
Like insect colonies.

00:29:03.441 --> 00:29:05.170
They even have a queen.

00:29:06.978 --> 00:29:09.572
That sounds terrifying.

00:29:09.647 --> 00:29:13.014
Captain Janeway hasn't been able
to destroy them.

00:29:13.084 --> 00:29:15.848
She is a Starfleet officer,

00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:18.514
trained to avoid violence
whenever possible.

00:29:18.590 --> 00:29:21.359
She would make peace
with the Borg, if she could.

00:29:21.426 --> 00:29:25.658
This is what I need...

00:29:25.730 --> 00:29:26.890
an enemy,

00:29:26.965 --> 00:29:29.695
someone to stand in the way

00:29:29.768 --> 00:29:32.168
of Voyager
finding B'Elanna Torres. It...

00:29:33.671 --> 00:29:36.071
Captain Janeway,
driven by vengeance

00:29:36.141 --> 00:29:38.268
must seek out
the Queen of the Borg.

00:29:38.343 --> 00:29:43.212
The audience thinks she plans
to destroy them all, but...

00:29:43.281 --> 00:29:45.146
Go on.

00:29:45.216 --> 00:29:47.013
The sudden reversal!

00:29:47.085 --> 00:29:50.020
Eh, Captain Janeway, holding
her spear at the queen's throat,

00:29:50.088 --> 00:29:51.316
throws her weapon aside,

00:29:51.389 --> 00:29:54.324
and she argues passionately

00:29:54.392 --> 00:29:56.553
to put an end
to their conflict...

00:29:56.628 --> 00:29:58.220
in words...

00:29:59.964 --> 00:30:02.489
...no one will fail
to understand.

00:30:02.567 --> 00:30:04.831
Including your patron?

00:30:10.308 --> 00:30:12.742
That's much better
than all that kissing.

00:30:20.819 --> 00:30:23.754
Stay and help me.

00:30:23.822 --> 00:30:25.449
I still need an ending.

00:30:25.523 --> 00:30:27.923
You'll figure something out.

00:30:27.992 --> 00:30:31.689
B'Elanna Torres dies tragically.

00:30:33.464 --> 00:30:35.591
You wouldn't dare.

00:30:59.157 --> 00:31:02.251
I followed you here
expecting to find a love nest.

00:31:05.897 --> 00:31:07.831
It's quite a nest.

00:31:10.902 --> 00:31:13.598
You're no poet
from across the sea.

00:31:13.671 --> 00:31:15.263
You're an Eternal.

00:31:16.908 --> 00:31:19.399
Maybe even B'Elanna Torres
herself.

00:31:19.477 --> 00:31:22.139
Don't be ridiculous.

00:31:22.213 --> 00:31:25.307
Mm.

00:31:25.383 --> 00:31:27.749
You know
all he thinks about is you?

00:31:29.354 --> 00:31:31.117
We're collaborators,

00:31:31.189 --> 00:31:32.451
that's all.

00:31:32.523 --> 00:31:35.083
If you come to the performance
tomorrow night,

00:31:35.159 --> 00:31:38.060
I'll expose you to the Autarch.

00:31:38.129 --> 00:31:40.620
Just leave us alone.

00:31:40.698 --> 00:31:43.599
You fix your ship and go.

00:31:43.668 --> 00:31:44.635
Please.

00:31:50.875 --> 00:31:52.137
Friend of yours?

00:31:54.946 --> 00:31:56.140
Harry?

00:31:59.317 --> 00:32:00.443
Give me a hand.

00:32:00.518 --> 00:32:01.883
Here.

00:32:01.953 --> 00:32:03.818
Oh, how?

00:32:03.888 --> 00:32:06.186
I ran into some turbulence
in the escape pod,

00:32:06.257 --> 00:32:08.885
decided to turn around
and follow your ion trail,

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:11.485
landed about 200 kilometers
from here.

00:32:11.562 --> 00:32:12.494
You walked?

00:32:12.563 --> 00:32:13.552
At night.

00:32:13.631 --> 00:32:15.292
I tracked your position
with a tricorder

00:32:15.366 --> 00:32:17.197
and tried to stay hidden
during the day.

00:32:18.503 --> 00:32:21.495
Uh, I've got
some emergency rations left,

00:32:21.572 --> 00:32:22.732
a phaser,

00:32:22.807 --> 00:32:24.570
and the escape pod's
transmitter,

00:32:24.642 --> 00:32:26.701
which I didn't have enough
power left to run, but...

00:32:26.778 --> 00:32:29.212
Harry Kim saves the day.

00:32:30.081 --> 00:32:32.641
Just the ending
I was looking for.

00:32:32.717 --> 00:32:35.345
Huh?

00:32:46.264 --> 00:32:47.322
The final moment.

00:32:47.398 --> 00:32:49.798
The last scene.

00:32:49.867 --> 00:32:52.836
More important than anything
that's gone before.

00:32:55.106 --> 00:32:56.539
But what is it?

00:33:08.953 --> 00:33:10.284
Where is she?

00:33:10.355 --> 00:33:11.845
Your collaborator's probably

00:33:11.923 --> 00:33:13.891
halfway across
the Eastern Sea by now.

00:33:13.958 --> 00:33:16.483
She'll be here.

00:33:16.561 --> 00:33:20.019
You said we'd have an ending
by mid-morning.

00:33:20.098 --> 00:33:22.532
We won't have time to learn it.

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:23.931
It'll come to me.

00:33:24.035 --> 00:33:25.332
Don't worry.

00:33:36.547 --> 00:33:38.276
Want to give it a try?

00:33:38.349 --> 00:33:40.943
Why not?

00:33:41.052 --> 00:33:43.612
The 38th time
might be the charm.

00:33:51.996 --> 00:33:53.463
It's working!

00:33:53.531 --> 00:33:55.726
The subspace transmitter
is on line.

00:33:57.101 --> 00:33:58.625
Why don't you do the honors?

00:33:58.703 --> 00:34:01.433
Voyager...

00:34:01.506 --> 00:34:03.599
this is the Delta Flyer.

00:34:07.645 --> 00:34:09.943
Our patron has arrived.

00:34:11.749 --> 00:34:14.183
He's not in a very good mood.

00:34:14.252 --> 00:34:15.913
He will be.

00:34:16.020 --> 00:34:17.817
Not if this is any indication.

00:34:17.889 --> 00:34:20.323
Yes. Kelis, this is
no way to end a play.

00:34:20.391 --> 00:34:21.983
It doesn't make sense.

00:34:24.062 --> 00:34:26.189
It'll have to.

00:34:26.264 --> 00:34:27.959
Go, go.

00:34:37.675 --> 00:34:41.543
Who are the enemies of Voyager?

00:34:41.612 --> 00:34:42.874
The Borg...

00:34:42.947 --> 00:34:44.881
Species 8472...

00:34:44.949 --> 00:34:47.509
You know where the ridge ends
just below the peak?

00:34:47.585 --> 00:34:49.610
Run there as fast as you can.

00:34:49.687 --> 00:34:53.145
You'll find a vessel
wrecked against the rocks.

00:34:53.224 --> 00:34:55.954
Go inside and give this
to our friend.

00:34:56.027 --> 00:34:57.358
Don't be frightened.

00:34:57.428 --> 00:34:58.554
Go.

00:35:22.653 --> 00:35:23.677
Tuvok.

00:35:28.626 --> 00:35:29.684
Tuvok.

00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:31.660
As you were.

00:35:40.605 --> 00:35:42.596
Bridge to Chakotay.

00:35:42.673 --> 00:35:44.265
Go ahead.

00:35:44.342 --> 00:35:46.776
Request permission
to be relieved.

00:35:46.844 --> 00:35:49.574
Understood.
I'll be right there.

00:35:55.119 --> 00:35:57.519
We're picking up
a subspace transmission...

00:35:57.588 --> 00:35:58.953
Starfleet frequency.

00:35:59.056 --> 00:36:00.819
It's a little rough.
Hang on.

00:36:05.163 --> 00:36:06.528
... Delta Flyer.

00:36:06.597 --> 00:36:08.087
Harry and I are all right.

00:36:08.166 --> 00:36:10.327
We're on an L-Class planet.

00:36:10.401 --> 00:36:12.301
Propulsion is down...

00:36:14.305 --> 00:36:15.897
Origin?

00:36:16.040 --> 00:36:17.507
5.2 light-years.

00:36:17.575 --> 00:36:19.099
F-type star.

00:36:19.177 --> 00:36:20.576
Looks like the fourth planet.

00:36:20.645 --> 00:36:22.670
Lay in a course...

00:36:22.747 --> 00:36:24.408
maximum warp.

00:36:24.482 --> 00:36:26.006
Seven of Nine.

00:36:26.083 --> 00:36:27.015
Captain.

00:36:27.084 --> 00:36:29.416
The Delta Flyer
has been found...

00:36:29.487 --> 00:36:32.479
in pieces on a rocky shore.

00:36:32.557 --> 00:36:34.047
And B'Elanna Torres?

00:36:34.125 --> 00:36:36.559
No sign of her.

00:36:36.627 --> 00:36:38.925
Seven of Nine, you are
my eyes and my ears.

00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:41.294
If anyone can find her,
it is you.

00:36:42.833 --> 00:36:47.497
Her eyes and her ears...

00:36:47.572 --> 00:36:50.439
and the viper in her nest.

00:36:50.508 --> 00:36:52.373
I, Seven of Nine,
have no intention

00:36:52.443 --> 00:36:54.741
of finding B'Elanna Torres.

00:36:54.812 --> 00:36:58.646
I, Seven of Nine,
am Queen of the Borg.

00:36:58.716 --> 00:36:59.910
Surprised?

00:36:59.984 --> 00:37:01.474
No one will be more surprised

00:37:01.552 --> 00:37:05.613
than Janeway when I take
my revenge on Voyager.

00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:06.884
Say nothing

00:37:06.991 --> 00:37:10.290
or you, too,
will be assimilated.

00:37:13.030 --> 00:37:15.055
Captain...

00:37:15.132 --> 00:37:16.497
I will comply.

00:37:21.839 --> 00:37:23.568
My enemies are everywhere...

00:37:23.641 --> 00:37:26.906
without and within.

00:37:26.978 --> 00:37:30.675
Seven of Nine is
Queen of the Borg.

00:37:30.748 --> 00:37:33.615
Surprised?

00:37:33.684 --> 00:37:35.914
So was I.

00:37:36.020 --> 00:37:41.788
Tell her nothing,
or I will lose my advantage...

00:37:41.859 --> 00:37:45.351
and my ship as well.

00:37:45.429 --> 00:37:46.919
Are you okay?

00:37:47.031 --> 00:37:47.929
Yes.

00:37:48.032 --> 00:37:48.930
We're fine.

00:37:49.033 --> 00:37:50.398
Good to hear it.

00:37:50.468 --> 00:37:51.935
We'll see you soon.

00:38:04.582 --> 00:38:05.810
Don't be afraid.

00:38:25.303 --> 00:38:26.292
What is it?

00:38:30.007 --> 00:38:32.498
"Without inspiration...

00:38:32.576 --> 00:38:34.942
B'Elanna Torres will perish."

00:38:36.547 --> 00:38:38.412
He's threatening
to kill off B'Elanna.

00:38:39.583 --> 00:38:42.313
As the climax to his play.

00:38:42.386 --> 00:38:43.683
Let him.

00:38:43.754 --> 00:38:45.551
That means...

00:38:45.623 --> 00:38:47.750
that he still can't
figure out the ending.

00:38:47.825 --> 00:38:49.019
Uh, who cares?!

00:38:49.093 --> 00:38:51.084
I do.

00:38:51.162 --> 00:38:52.459
You're serious.

00:38:54.432 --> 00:38:55.694
Harry...

00:38:57.134 --> 00:38:59.125
...have you ever
inspired anybody?

00:38:59.203 --> 00:39:01.398
That's kind
of a strange question.

00:39:01.472 --> 00:39:04.032
Well, it's been
a strange couple of weeks.

00:39:04.108 --> 00:39:05.598
He needs me, or he's the one

00:39:05.676 --> 00:39:07.337
who's going to die
on that stage.

00:39:07.411 --> 00:39:09.345
What are you talking about?

00:39:09.413 --> 00:39:11.813
The transporter is on line.

00:39:11.882 --> 00:39:13.509
Tell the Captain
I'll be a little late.

00:39:13.584 --> 00:39:14.881
B'Elanna?

00:39:15.019 --> 00:39:17.385
Wait for my signal.

00:39:24.862 --> 00:39:26.727
My death is irrelevant.

00:39:26.797 --> 00:39:28.890
You will never see
the gleaming cities of Earth.

00:39:28.999 --> 00:39:30.899
You will be assimilated.

00:39:31.001 --> 00:39:32.901
And if I let you live?

00:39:33.037 --> 00:39:35.267
Also irrelevant.

00:39:35.339 --> 00:39:38.172
You don't believe that.

00:39:41.178 --> 00:39:42.839
The battle is over.

00:39:42.913 --> 00:39:45.211
Go home.

00:39:45.282 --> 00:39:47.182
How foolish of you
to let me go...

00:39:47.251 --> 00:39:48.684
free to attack you again.

00:39:48.753 --> 00:39:51.347
And again and again,

00:39:51.422 --> 00:39:54.357
until all your drones and
all my crew are destroyed...

00:39:54.425 --> 00:39:56.325
until everything
we value is gone

00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:59.329
and there is nothing left...

00:39:59.397 --> 00:40:01.126
but our hatred.

00:40:03.534 --> 00:40:05.399
This final scene
will ruin everything

00:40:05.469 --> 00:40:06.731
that we've done out there.

00:40:06.804 --> 00:40:08.237
We'll have to improvise.

00:40:08.305 --> 00:40:09.237
It's too late.

00:40:09.306 --> 00:40:10.466
No, it's not.

00:40:10.541 --> 00:40:12.133
I knew you'd come.

00:40:12.209 --> 00:40:13.471
And I told you not to.

00:40:13.544 --> 00:40:14.511
Wait!

00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:17.908
Let's go.

00:40:19.717 --> 00:40:25.383
Finally, Voyager
has reached our shores.

00:40:25.456 --> 00:40:28.220
And not a moment too soon.

00:40:28.292 --> 00:40:30.852
Kelis the Poet must say good-bye

00:40:30.928 --> 00:40:35.831
as B'Elanna Torres returns
to the Eternals

00:40:35.900 --> 00:40:38.164
in a dazzling blaze of light.

00:40:39.770 --> 00:40:42.364
On a faraway,
snow-covered peak...

00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:43.566
No!

00:40:43.641 --> 00:40:45.973
Right here, before your eyes.

00:40:46.076 --> 00:40:48.408
Wait. She's not
from across the Eastern Sea.

00:40:48.479 --> 00:40:50.208
She's an Eternal.

00:40:50.281 --> 00:40:52.146
I'm telling you
she's B'Elanna Torres.

00:40:52.216 --> 00:40:53.683
The real B'Elanna Torres!

00:40:53.751 --> 00:40:55.150
I saw her ship!

00:40:56.754 --> 00:41:02.556
The lead actress,
in a fit of jealousy

00:41:02.626 --> 00:41:04.890
brands her rival an Eternal.

00:41:04.962 --> 00:41:08.830
Our patron rises to his feet
to stop the play.

00:41:18.108 --> 00:41:19.541
Nicely done.

00:41:22.480 --> 00:41:24.710
I almost believed you.

00:41:26.851 --> 00:41:27.875
Continue.

00:41:35.493 --> 00:41:37.654
Stay.

00:41:37.728 --> 00:41:39.093
Voyager needs me.

00:41:41.265 --> 00:41:42.892
So do I.

00:41:42.967 --> 00:41:44.434
No, you don't.

00:41:46.203 --> 00:41:48.694
You have all that you need
right here.

00:41:54.311 --> 00:41:56.279
I'll be inspired...

00:41:59.917 --> 00:42:02.715
...every time I think of you.

00:42:04.588 --> 00:42:05.885
One to beam...

00:42:08.125 --> 00:42:10.286
...to ascend...

00:42:10.361 --> 00:42:12.829
to the heavens.

00:42:19.637 --> 00:42:21.104
And so ends

00:42:21.171 --> 00:42:23.036
The Rescue of B'Elanna Torres,

00:42:23.107 --> 00:42:26.543
half-Klingon, B'Elanna Torres,
half-human,

00:42:26.610 --> 00:42:30.603
B'Elanna Torres, Chief Engineer.

00:42:30.681 --> 00:42:34.276
These stories will continue...

00:42:34.351 --> 00:42:36.876
for as long as we have
the breath to tell them...

00:42:38.656 --> 00:42:41.557
...and as long as our patrons...

00:42:41.625 --> 00:42:43.115
remain wise

00:42:43.193 --> 00:42:45.559
and compassionate.

00:42:45.629 --> 00:42:47.529
And Voyager
will continue on her journey

00:42:47.598 --> 00:42:50.692
to the gleaming cities
of Earth...

00:42:50.768 --> 00:42:52.793
where peace reigns...

00:42:52.870 --> 00:42:55.862
and hatred has no home.
